Subject: [PATCH] HID: ipts: correct the EDS1 raw report descriptor size

The EDS1 fallback descriptor defines a two-byte scan time followed by
7485 bytes of constant data for report 0x41. Including the report ID,
this describes a 7488-byte report. However, ipts_resources_init()
allocates 7485 bytes and ipts_hid_input_data() submits 7485 bytes.

HID core now checks the supplied buffer size and rejects every raw
report with -EINVAL before it reaches hidraw. On a Surface Pro 6 the
warning reports 7487 expected payload bytes versus 7484 available.
Older HID core padded the mismatch, potentially beyond the allocation.

Set the constant data count to 7482, accounting for the two scan-time
bytes and report ID. This matches the existing allocation and wire
format without changing payload offsets or the userspace protocol.
Native EDS2 descriptors are unaffected.

Tested on a Surface Pro 6 (045E:001F) with 7.2.9 using an equivalent
one-byte HID-BPF descriptor correction: raw reports changed from
-EINVAL to success, iptsd 3.1.0 received data, and simultaneous contact
slots were recorded. No iptsd configuration changes were required.

---
diff --git a/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h b/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h
--- a/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h
+++ b/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
 	0x81, 0x02,	  /*      Input (Variable),              */
 	0x09, 0x61,	  /*      Usage (Gesture Char Quality),  */
 	0x75, 0x08,	  /*      Report Size (8),               */
-	0x96, 0x3D, 0x1D, /*      Report Count (7485),           */
+	0x96, 0x3A, 0x1D, /*      Report Count (7482),           */
 	0x81, 0x03,	  /*      Input (Constant, Variable),    */
 	0x85, 0x42,	  /*      Report ID (66),                */
 	0x06, 0x00, 0xFF, /*      Usage Page (FF00h),            */
